WEBVTT

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:02.514
{happy}Hello, and welcome to Shah Spectrum.

00:00:02.514 --> 00:00:04.392
If you're new here, welcome.

00:00:04.392 --> 00:00:08.365
If you're back again, it's lovely to have you with us.

00:00:08.365 --> 00:00:15.360
{happy}Over one weekend, Iran said it fired drones at a base in Bahrain, and that

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.606
tankers had hit mines near the Strait of Hormuz.

00:00:17.606 --> 00:00:21.065
So what is actually confirmed, and what is only a claim?

00:00:21.065 --> 00:00:23.136
{happy}Hi, I'm Mittal Shah.

00:00:23.136 --> 00:00:26.475
Stay with me for a few minutes, and we'll separate the two.

00:00:26.475 --> 00:00:28.311
{fluent}First, Bahrain.

00:00:28.311 --> 00:00:34.113
On the fifteenth of November, Iran's Revolutionary Guard, its elite armed force,

00:00:34.113 --> 00:00:39.558
said six drones hit a United States radar at a base in al-Riffa, in Bahrain.

00:00:39.558 --> 00:00:45.870
Bahrain's defence force said it had intercepted multiple Iranian aerial attacks.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:50.939
Two days earlier, on the thirteenth, the United States military's Central Command

00:00:50.939 --> 00:00:54.918
had called a similar Iranian claim about a Bahrain radar false:

00:00:54.918 --> 00:00:58.085
two drones were shot down, with no damage.

00:00:58.085 --> 00:00:59.943
So the pattern so far:

00:00:59.943 --> 00:01:04.728
Iran says it hit something, and the other side says it stopped the attacks.

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:06.436
Now, the sea.

00:01:06.436 --> 00:01:12.492
Iran's Revolutionary Guard said two oil tankers struck mines on a southern route

00:01:12.492 --> 00:01:13.963
that Iran had not authorised.

00:01:13.963 --> 00:01:18.829
One, it said, was a supertanker carrying more than two million barrels of oil, and

00:01:18.829 --> 00:01:19.429
it sank.

00:01:19.321 --> 00:01:24.234
Iran's navy separately said a tanker caught fire east of the strait.

00:01:24.234 --> 00:01:30.450
State television spoke of five vessels within forty-eight hours, and another account

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:31.050
said three.

00:01:30.941 --> 00:01:32.317
That is the problem.

00:01:32.317 --> 00:01:36.643
The counts differ, and none of the reports we read gave ship names.

00:01:36.643 --> 00:01:42.552
A British maritime monitor said the damage was unknown and the crew were safe.

00:01:42.552 --> 00:01:48.531
It was also aware of an Indian shipping report of a tanker attack in the Gulf, but

00:01:48.531 --> 00:01:50.631
could not say whether it was the same incident.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.969
Why does a mine matter so much?

00:01:53.969 --> 00:02:00.117
In general, a sea mine is a cheap explosive that sits in the water and goes off when

00:02:00.117 --> 00:02:01.404
a ship touches it.

00:02:01.404 --> 00:02:04.252
Even a few mines, or the fear of them, can slow shipping.

00:02:04.252 --> 00:02:09.993
In general, insurers then charge more, and captains choose other routes or wait.

00:02:09.993 --> 00:02:14.785
The Strait of Hormuz is the narrow channel that carries about a fifth of the world's

00:02:14.785 --> 00:02:18.504
oil in normal times, so worry there is felt far away.

00:02:19.289 --> 00:02:23.168
The United States tells a different story about the sea.

00:02:23.168 --> 00:02:27.959
It says it has helped Gulf countries export one and a half billion barrels through

00:02:27.959 --> 00:02:32.819
the strait since the summer, and that the main routes have been cleared of mines.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:37.451
These are different claims, and we cannot yet say how they fit together.

00:02:38.236 --> 00:02:39.149
Now the numbers.

00:02:39.149 --> 00:02:45.103
The International Energy Agency, the group that tracks global energy, said in its

00:02:45.103 --> 00:02:49.677
November report that Gulf oil exports, not counting Oman, were eighteen point four

00:02:49.677 --> 00:02:51.630
million barrels a day.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:55.927
That is twenty-six per cent below the level before the war.

00:02:55.927 --> 00:03:00.885
Yet it also said that, in October, world oil supply was higher than demand for the

00:03:00.885 --> 00:03:02.860
first time since the war began.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:07.006
And on the thirteenth, Brent, the global benchmark price for oil, was about

00:03:07.006 --> 00:03:08.981
ninety-six dollars a barrel.

00:03:09.865 --> 00:03:11.336
What do we not know?

00:03:11.336 --> 00:03:16.428
Whether any ship was really sunk, since those claims come only from Iran.

00:03:16.428 --> 00:03:17.652
How many were hit.

00:03:17.652 --> 00:03:19.245
And where talks stand.

00:03:19.245 --> 00:03:25.198
Iran's foreign ministry has ruled out limiting its uranium enrichment as a basis for

00:03:25.198 --> 00:03:25.798
a deal.

00:03:25.656 --> 00:03:30.038
The American president has said, "we don't need a deal with Iran." A news agency

00:03:30.038 --> 00:03:35.636
reported that he is weighing whether to hold off on strikes unless there is a new

00:03:35.636 --> 00:03:36.610
provocation.

00:03:37.469 --> 00:03:38.314
To sum up:

00:03:38.314 --> 00:03:41.022
the facts are thin and the claims are loud.

00:03:41.022 --> 00:03:44.409
Iran says it attacked Bahrain and mined ships.

00:03:44.409 --> 00:03:49.654
Bahrain says it intercepted attacks, and the United States military says the main

00:03:49.654 --> 00:03:51.654
sea routes are clear.

00:03:51.654 --> 00:03:56.526
What we can say is that the risk around Hormuz is back in the headlines.

00:03:56.526 --> 00:03:59.563
Oil prices are one measure of that risk.

00:04:00.322 --> 00:04:03.913
Before you go, we have covered this story before.

00:04:03.913 --> 00:04:08.108
On the twenty-ninth of October, our episode 'Hormuz and oil:

00:04:08.108 --> 00:04:12.003
what it means for India' explained why the strait matters.

00:04:12.003 --> 00:04:16.187
And on the eleventh of November, 'Oil below ninety dollars:

00:04:16.187 --> 00:04:20.361
what a falling barrel means for India' looked at how the price fell.

00:04:20.361 --> 00:04:22.481
The links are in the description.

00:04:22.481 --> 00:04:25.702
{happy}Thanks for listening, and see you in the next episode!

